okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Session backup: git worktrees as an option (default off) and a per-folder choice of the work folder's first-level folders, in menu 18."
requested: "User, 2026-10-10: '백업에 워크트리리는 선택옵션. 또 하위폴더에있는 첫번째 레벨의 폴더를 선택해서 백업가능하게..'; answers: worktree default '포함 안 함', folder choice '체크 해제한 것만 제외' (new folders are included)."
before: "Worktrees inside the work folder were always backed up as plain files (this repo: .claude/worktrees, 2, 45 MB); worktrees elsewhere never. Excludes were name patterns at any depth, so leaving out 'data' also dropped src/data."
changes:
  collect: "session_backup_collect: is_linked_worktree (a .git FILE whose gitdir points into .../worktrees/; submodules point into modules/ and stay), git_worktrees / outside_worktrees (git worktree list --porcelain), CollectOptions.skip_top + worktrees ('off'|'inside'|'all'), add_tree skips first-level folders ('not selected') and linked worktrees ('worktree'), CollectRoots.worktrees -> extra roots worktree-1.. recorded in manifest roots; measure_tree follows the same choices."
  cli_ops: "backup create reads settings['folders'][<workspace digest>] = {skip_top, worktrees}; --worktrees off|inside|all overrides once; preflight measures the same way (plus outside worktrees); result 'left_out' {folders, worktrees, worktree_mode, outside_worktrees}; choices are not counted as 'not backed up'. destination_roots includes worktree-N roots, restored to their original paths."
  restore_fix: "session_backup_ops._atomic_write: Windows refuses os.replace onto a read-only file (git object files are read-only) - seen as 'PermissionError: [WinError 5] Access is denied ... .git\\objects\\85\\...' when restoring a work folder with .git. Now the file is made writable and the replace retried. A test fails without the fix and passes with it."
  menu: "Section '── Work folder: first-level folders (Enter: back up / leave out) ──': 'Git worktrees [off · N in this folder · M elsewhere]' (Enter cycles off -> inside -> all), 'Measure folder sizes [measured MM-DD HH:MM]' (up to 20 s, sizes shown on rows), one '[x] name [backed up · size]' row per first-level folder (Enter toggles), '[-] name [left out by name (Exclude…)]' for name-pattern excludes, '[ ] name [git worktree · follows Git worktrees]' for a worktree at the first level; Back up now shows 'Left out by your choice: …' and 'Git worktrees: mode; N left out; M outside this folder included'."
tests: "tests/test_session_backup_folders.py 8 (worktree vs submodule detection; measure follows choices; default leaves worktrees out and keeps folders; menu toggles drive the next backup and only the first level; result lines in the menu; measured sizes on rows; read-only file restore; with git: --worktrees all backs up and restores an outside worktree in place). Groups: unit 1834 OK, runtime 402 OK, channel 457 OK, router 1188 OK; ruff clean; router 9611 200."
e2e: "evidence/e2e_folders.py (+ _steps.py): real git repo on G: with a worktree inside (.claude/worktrees/feat) and one outside; menu in conhost by key events. Run 15:22-15:23: section shows 'Git worktrees  [off · 1 in this folder · 1 elsewhere]'; Measure -> sizes; data -> '[ ] data  [left out'; Back up now -> 'Left out by your choice: 1 folder(s): data', 'Git worktrees: off; 1 left out' (snapshot files notes.md, src/data/keep.txt; left out data, .claude/worktrees/feat); Git worktrees -> inside -> all; Back up now -> 'Git worktrees: all; 1 outside this folder included' (snapshot roots include worktree-1 with outside-wip.txt; the inside worktree's files are in). 6 screenshots."
not_done: "Not committed, pushed or deployed."
